<div class="theme-card" id="conversation">
  <div class="theme-img"><img src="http://localhost:4000/images/slider7001400/web_audio_speech.png" alt="Spoken conversation analysis" loading="lazy" /></div>
  <div class="theme-text">
    <h3><span data-l="en">Spoken conversation analysis</span><span data-l="hi" lang="hi">बोली गई बातचीत का विश्लेषण</span></h3>
    <p class="theme-lead-hi" data-l="hi" lang="hi">बातचीत कैसे आगे बढ़ती है, यह समझने के लिए वाणी, चेहरे, साँस, हृदय और पुतली के संकेतों का अध्ययन।</p>
    <p>Spoken communication enables us to share thoughts, learn and create knowledge. Often we spend our day immersed in <em>listening to</em> or <em>speaking in</em> a conversation. Some conversations are quick and some <em>go on and on</em>, some start gradually and some end abruptly. Our goal is to explore spoken conversations by capturing and analyzing the speech, facial, breathing, heart and pupil signals of the participating individuals. This is a long-term effort involving building and testing several hypotheses, and gaining scientific insights into this amazing form of information transfer. Strength permitting, we will also analyze this aspect in bird (and animal) communication.</p>

    <div class="tags"><span>multi-channel data acquisition</span><span>signal processing</span><span>machine learning</span><span>experiment design</span><span>perception</span><span>cognition</span><span>foundation models</span></div>
    
