<div class="theme-card" id="audio-cognition">
  <div class="theme-img"><img src="http://localhost:4000/images/pubpic/web_paper_highlights_itd_ild_RT.png" alt="Audio cognition through behavioral experiments" loading="lazy" /></div>
  <div class="theme-text">
    <h3><span data-l="en">Audio cognition through behavioral experiments</span><span data-l="hi" lang="hi">व्यवहारिक प्रयोगों से श्रवण संज्ञान की समझ</span></h3>
    <p class="theme-lead-hi" data-l="hi" lang="hi">बटन दबाने और प्रतिक्रिया-समय से हम कैसे सुनते हैं, इसका पता चलता है।</p>
    <p>Unlike neuroimaging experiments like EEG and fMRI, behavioral experiments capture simple responses such as a button press or reaction time during a live experiment. When carefully captured, these simple responses can be analyzed to understand human cognition. We have explored talker perception, the impact of language on talker perception, and, currently, spatial cognition. We look forward to translating these findings into AI algorithms.</p>

