<div class="theme-card" id="healthcare">
  <div class="theme-img"><img src="http://localhost:4000/images/pubpic/web_paper_highlights_coswara_creation.png" alt="Data analysis for human healthcare" loading="lazy" /></div>
  <div class="theme-text">
    <h3><span data-l="en">Data analysis for human healthcare</span><span data-l="hi" lang="hi">मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए डेटा विश्लेषण</span></h3>
    <p class="theme-lead-hi" data-l="hi" lang="hi">दूरस्थ, कम लागत वाली रोग-जाँच के लिए साँस, खाँसी और वाणी को सुनना।</p>
    <p>Do you recall a doctor listening to body sounds using a stethoscope? The art of listening to body sounds is called <em>auscultation</em> and dates back to the 1820s. We aim to extract more information from body sounds using signal processing and machine learning, towards remote, cost-effective, and scalable disease screening. We have analyzed respiratory sounds such as breathing, cough and speech collected during the pandemic from individuals with and without COVID-19, and released them openly as the Coswara dataset. Our ANRF-funded project <em>Melodies of the Lungs</em> takes this towards AI-based point-of-care respiratory healthcare.</p>

    <div class="tags"><span>respiratory acoustics</span><span>time-series analysis</span><span>audio signal processing</span><span>machine learning</span><span>inferential statistics</span><span>web development</span><span>biosciences</span></div>
    
